 # Preview Specifications
 
+## Request and Cache Lifecycle
+
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-001**: When a request identifies an unknown clip revision, the system SHALL return 404 without enqueuing a render job.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-002**: When the requested preview is cached, the system SHALL return 200 with the JPEG for the requested revision and renderer version.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+
+## 2Q Eviction Policy
+
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-QA-001**: When a completed preview is admitted to the cache for the first time, the system SHALL place it in the cold queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-QA-002**: When a request retrieves a preview from the cold queue, the system SHALL promote that entry to the hot queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-QA-003**: The cache SHALL divide its 12 GiB capacity between cold and hot queues, reserving a tuning parameter (initially 80% for hot, 20% for cold) for each allocation.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-QA-004**: When the cold queue exceeds its allocation, the system SHALL evict cold entries in FIFO order (oldest first) to stay within the cold queue's allocation.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-QA-005**: When the hot queue exceeds its allocation, the system SHALL evict hot entries in FIFO order (oldest first) to stay within the hot queue's allocation.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-QA-006**: When evicting to free space for a new cold entry, the system SHALL evict from the cold queue first; if the cold queue is empty or insufficient, the system SHALL borrow space from the hot queue's allocation to bring the total cache below 12 GiB.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-QA-007**: The system SHALL never evict an entry that has concurrent pending requests for it, even if eviction would free space; instead, eviction waits until deduplication is complete.
